  - HSDS
  - open data
abstract: >-
  A curated, source-anchored directory of help and support services across the
  United States, resolved to the city and town level — food assistance, shelter
  and housing, treatment, recovery and support meetings, crisis lines, domestic
  violence programs, veteran services, LGBTQ+ centers, legal aid, free clinics,
  disability and refugee services, and childcare. Roughly 260,000 records
  (12,947 organizations, 136,038 service locations, 77,714 recurring meetings)
  across 32,307 US places, each citing at least one of 251 first-class source
  records and carrying a verification stamp with the date it was last checked.
  Assembled from US federal open data, open community feeds (the BMLT ecosystem
  for NA; Meeting Guide/TSML feeds for AA; SMART, ACA, Nar-Anon, Overeaters
  Anonymous, Gamblers Anonymous and others), and facts-only re-expression of
  national nonprofit network directories. Ships with a JSON Schema, an
  independent validation gate, an Open Referral HSDS 3.0 export, a datasheet
  following Gebru et al., and a documented rights posture that includes the
  sources deliberately not collected because their terms prohibit it.
  Confidential domestic violence shelter locations are never published, and
  recovery meeting records carry venue and schedule facts only.
